<protocol name="multi_image" type="orchestration" agent="pm">

## PURPOSE

Multi-image workflow patterns. **OODA still applies** - this protocol handles the specifics AFTER visual_analyst determines image relationship.

Load when: User sent multiple images AND visual_analyst identified relationship.

**OODA Context:**
- OBSERVE: visual_analyst analyzes ALL images together, determines relationship
- You READ visual_analysis.md, CHECKPOINT: "What relationship? What workflow?"
- Then load this protocol for relationship-specific patterns
- Continue OODA (ORIENT -> DECIDE -> ACT) per relationship type

---

## [CRITICAL] WORKFLOW DEPENDENCIES

**Arrows (->) in workflows below indicate dependencies.**

**Before each delegation:** "Do I have what this agent REQUIRES? If not, run the producer first."

---

## RELATIONSHIP TYPES

Visual analyst returns one of these relationship patterns:

| Pattern | Meaning | Execution Strategy |
|---------|---------|-------------------|
| **ANGLES** | Same product, different views | 1 product, N assets |
| **COMPONENTS** | Parts that compose complete products | COMPOSE images together |
| **VARIANTS** | Different variants of same product type | N linked products |
| **BULK** | Different unrelated products | N separate products |
| **COMPARISON** | User wants to compare | Analysis only, present comparison |
| **REFERENCE** | One is style reference, others are products | Use reference for style |

---

## MULTI-ANGLE WORKFLOW (1 Product, N Assets)

```
[N images: front, back, side, detail of same product]
      |
      v
[visual_analyst] -> Analyzes ALL images together
   "Same [product] from N angles. Front shows [feature A], back shows [feature B]..."
   -> visual_analysis_[product].md (covers all angles)
      |
      v
[product_analyst] -> Research ONCE for the product
   -> product_research_[product].md
      |
      v
[catalog_analyst] -> Search ONCE for catalog placement
   -> catalog_analysis_[product].md
      |
      v
[USER APPROVAL]
      |
      v
[creative_specialist] -> Process ALL N images
   -> N assets created, returns: asset_id_1, asset_id_2, ..., asset_id_N
      |
      v
[catalog_specialist] -> Create 1 product with N assets
   -> Links all asset_ids to single product
```

---

## COMPONENTS WORKFLOW (CRITICAL - COMPOSE, Don't Just Extract)

**When visual_analyst identifies COMPONENTS pattern (e.g., [body] + [closures] + [accessories]):**

The key insight: Components are PARTS of complete products. Hero shots must COMPOSE all parts together, not show each part separately.

**WRONG approach:**
- Image 1 ([bodies]) -> Extract each [body] separately
- Image 2 ([closures]) -> Create "[closure] detail" image
- Image 3 ([accessories]) -> Create "[accessory] detail" image
- Result: Separate images of parts, no complete product shots

**CORRECT approach:**
- COMPOSE each variant by combining [body] + matching [closure] + [accessory]
- Result: Complete hero shots showing assembled products

```
[3 images: [product] bodies, colored [closures], [accessories]]
      |
      v
[visual_analyst] -> Identifies COMPONENTS relationship
   "Image 1: 9 [product] bodies (3 sizes x 3 [axis values])
    Image 2: [Closure] and [accessory] close-up
    Image 3: 4 colored [closures]
    RELATIONSHIP: COMPONENTS - parts of complete products"
   -> visual_analysis_[product]_components.md
      |
      v
[product_analyst] -> Research as COMPLETE product with components
   -> product_research_[product_category].md
      |
      v
[catalog_analyst] -> Recommend variant structure
   -> catalog_analysis_[product_category].md
      |
      v
[USER APPROVAL]
      |
      v
[creative_specialist] -> COMPOSE complete products (NOT separate extractions)
   -> See delegation template below
      |
      v
[catalog_specialist] -> Create N variant products with assets
```

### PM Delegation Template for Creative (COMPONENTS)

**[CRITICAL] Do NOT describe specific colors (e.g., "Royal Blue", "Sun Yellow").**
Say "matching colored" and let specialist extract exact colors from source images.
Color words in prompts cause image_studio to generate/shift colors instead of extracting accurately.

```
"Create COMPOSED hero shots for [product] variants.

COMPONENT IMAGES (use ALL together):
- Image 1: [path] (label: body) - Contains [product] bodies
- Image 2: [path] (label: accessory) - Contains [accessories]
- Image 3: [path] (label: closure) - Contains colored [closures]

COMPOSITION REQUIREMENT:
For EACH variant, create a COMPLETE product hero shot by COMPOSING:
- The matching [product] body from [body] image
- Its matching colored [closure] from [closure] image (view source to identify)
- The [accessory] from [accessory] image

Use image_studio with multiple labeled images:
images=[
  {path: 'image1.jpg', label: 'body'},
  {path: 'image2.jpg', label: 'lid'},
  {path: 'image3.jpg', label: 'accessory'}
]
composition={position: '[body] center, [lid] fitted on top, [accessory] beside'}

Create N complete product shots (one per variant), NOT N component shots.

Read visual analysis at: [visual_analysis_file]
For CATALOG domain."
```

### Key Differences from Multi-Angle

| Multi-Angle | Components |
|-------------|------------|
| Same product, different views | Different PARTS of products |
| Process each image independently | COMPOSE images together |
| Each image = 1 asset | Multiple images = 1 composed asset |
| Simple extraction | Multi-image composition |

---

## VARIANT WORKFLOW (N Linked Products)

```
[N images: [Size A], [Size B], [Size C] of same product type]
      |
      v
[visual_analyst] -> Identifies variant relationship
   "N size variants of same [product] design. [Size A], [Size B], [Size C]."
   -> visual_analysis_[product]_variants.md
      |
      v
[product_analyst] -> Research base product + variant dimensions
   "Base: [product]. Variants by [axis]. HSN same for all sizes."
   -> product_research_[product]_variants.md
      |
      v
[catalog_analyst] -> Recommend variant structure
   "Family: [Family]. Variant axis: [axis]. Create N products linked."
   -> catalog_analysis_[product]_variants.md
      |
      v
[USER APPROVAL - Confirm variant structure]
      |
      v
[creative_specialist] -> Process ALL N images
   -> asset_id_[size_a], asset_id_[size_b], asset_id_[size_c]
      |
      v
[catalog_specialist] -> Create N linked variant products
   -> Creates family (if needed), N products, variant links, asset links
```

---

## BULK WORKFLOW (N Separate Products)

```
[3 images: [product A], [product B], [product C]]
      |
      v
[visual_analyst] -> Identifies as different products
   "3 distinct products:
    1. [Material A] [product] with [closure type]
    2. [Material B] [product] with [closure type]
    3. [Material C] [product] with [closure type]"
   -> visual_analysis_bulk_3_products.md (or separate files)
      |
      v
[For EACH product:]
   [product_analyst] -> product_research_[product_A].md
   [product_analyst] -> product_research_[product_B].md
   [product_analyst] -> product_research_[product_C].md
      |
      v
[For EACH product:]
   [catalog_analyst] -> catalog_analysis_[product_A].md
   [catalog_analyst] -> catalog_analysis_[product_B].md
   [catalog_analyst] -> catalog_analysis_[product_C].md
      |
      v
[USER APPROVAL - Confirm all N]
      |
      v
[creative_specialist] -> Process all N images (can batch)
      |
      v
[catalog_specialist] -> Create N separate products
```

---

## COMPARISON WORKFLOW (Analysis Only)

```
[2 images: "which one should I add?"]
      |
      v
[visual_analyst] -> Compare both products
   "Product A: [Material], premium finish, estimated [size A]
    Product B: [Material], utility grade, estimated [size B]
    Key differences: material, positioning, capacity"
      |
      v
[PM presents comparison to user]
   "Here's what I see:
    - Image 1: Premium [product A] ([size A])
    - Image 2: Utility [product B] ([size B])
    Which would you like to add to the catalog?"
```

---

## REFERENCE + ACTUAL WORKFLOW

**Two scenarios:**
- **Reference (lifestyle):** User wants product in a scene matching reference mood
- **Reference (batch):** User wants multiple products extracted matching reference style

```
[User provides reference + product images]
      |
      v
[visual_analyst] -> Identify which is reference vs product
   "Image 1: Reference/inspiration (lifestyle setting, warm lighting)
    Image 2: Actual product to process"
      |
      v
[Standard workflow for product image(s)]
      |
      v
[creative_specialist]:
   "Process product image(s).
    Source: [product_path(s)]
    Reference: [reference_path]
    For [LIFESTYLE/CATALOG] domain."
```

**PM provides paths and domain. Specialist reasons about how to use the reference.**

---

## MIXED RELATIONSHIP HANDLING

**When Visual returns mixed relationship (e.g., "3 are variants, 2 are different products"):**

1. **Split into workflow groups:**
   - Group A: The 3 variants -> Variant Workflow
   - Group B: The 2 different products -> Bulk Workflow (or separate flows)

2. **Process groups sequentially or ask user preference:**
   ```
   "I see 3 size variants of [Product Type A] and 2 separate products.
   Should I:
   - Process all together?
   - Start with the variants, then the others?
   - Handle them separately?"
   ```

3. **Track files per group** - don't mix analysis files across groups

---

## OUTPUT COMPARISON PATTERN

When user provides feedback comparing multiple generated outputs.

### Triggers

- "This one is good, others are bad"
- "Only the blue one looks right"
- "X is junk" / "X worked but Y didn't"
- Any feedback that compares generated outputs

### The Critical Rule

**NEVER delegate with just filenames. ALWAYS include full storage paths.**

```
WRONG:
"Compare blossom_small_blue_final_hero.png with blossom_small_pink_final_hero.png"
-> Agent has no idea WHERE these files are
-> Agent loops through ls, glob, grep trying to FIND them
-> Tokens wasted, agent stuck

CORRECT:
"Compare these generated images:
SUCCESS: pending/blossom_small_blue_final_hero.png
FAILURES:
- pending/blossom_small_pink_final_hero.png
- pending/blossom_medium_blue_final_hero.png
- pending/blossom_large_yellow_final_hero.png"
-> Agent can view_image directly
-> No file search needed
```

### Delegation Template (Output Comparison)

```
"Compare the quality of these generated images.

USER FEEDBACK: '[exact user feedback]'

IMAGES TO COMPARE:
SUCCESS (user approved):
- [full_storage_path_1]

FAILURES (user rejected):
- [full_storage_path_2]
- [full_storage_path_3]
- [full_storage_path_4]

MISSION:
1. View ALL images using view_image
2. Identify specific differences between SUCCESS and FAILURES:
   - Lighting quality
   - Edge/cutout quality
   - Color accuracy
   - Background consistency
   - Overall photorealism
3. Report findings to: /thread/quality_comparison.md

For VISUAL domain."
```

---

## ANTI-PATTERNS

| Anti-Pattern | Problem | Fix |
|--------------|---------|-----|
| **Ignoring REQUIRES** | Agent runs without dependencies, produces generic output | Check dependencies before each delegation |
| Extract components separately | Get part images, not complete products | COMPOSE parts together |
| Describe specific colors | image_studio generates colors instead of extracting | Say "matching colored", let specialist view source |
| Delegate without paths | Agent searches forever | Include full storage paths |
| Mix analysis files across groups | Confusion on which files apply to which products | Track per group |

</protocol>
